---
// Privacy is per platform and must stay per platform. Do not merge these into one reassuring sentence.
---
<dl class="privacy">
  <div>
    <dt>Ubuntu</dt>
    <dd>The search panel's cookies and storage are held in memory only and discarded when DNDReader quits.</dd>
  </div>
  <div>
    <dt>Windows</dt>
    <dd>Windows can't keep the panel's data in memory, so it uses a temporary folder that is cleared and deleted when you quit. During a session that data is on disk, and after a crash a leftover folder can remain until the next launch removes it.</dd>
  </div>
  <div>
    <dt>Android</dt>
    <dd>Android can't keep the panel's data in memory either, so it lives in the app's private storage while the app runs, where other apps can't read it. That storage is deleted the next time the app starts. It is not gone the moment you swipe the app away.</dd>
  </div>
</dl>
